 Data Model

The dataset consists of 4 main tables:

 1. Customers
Contains customer demographic and location data.

| Column | Description |
|--------|------------|
| customer_id | Unique ID for each customer |
| name | Customer name |
| location | City/Region |

 2. Orders
Represents each purchase transaction.

| Column | Description |
|--------|------------|
| order_id | Unique order ID |
| customer_id | Linked to Customers |
| order_date | Date of purchase |
| total_amount | Total order value |

 3. Products
Stores product-related information.

| Column | Description |
|--------|------------|
| product_id | Unique product ID |
| name | Product name |
| price | Product price |

 4. Orders_Details
Contains line-level transaction data.

| Column | Description |
|--------|------------|
| order_id | Linked to Orders |
| product_id | Linked to Products |
| quantity | Units sold |
| price_per_unit | Price per unit |
